  "weekLabel": "Week of Nov 23–27, 2026 (Thanksgiving week)",
  "headline": "No IPOs scheduled for Thanksgiving week after Anthropic's record $81.3B debut; ABGC and CORE wait in the wings",
  "summary": "Renaissance Capital shows no US IPOs scheduled for Nov 23–27, and Football Manager SPAC (FBLLU) postponed its Nov 20 deal. IPOScoop lists Tracx Logis (TRCX, 1M shares at $18–$22, ~$20M) and Primagrove (YNTE, $4–$6, ~$30.5M) for the week of Nov 30, single-source dates flagged unconfirmed; RegenLab USA (RGNA, 2.5M shares at $6–$8, ~$18M) has no public date. Renaissance expects two large filers to be eligible after the holiday: American Barrick Gold (ABGC, est. ~$6B) and the newly filed Core Specialty Insurance (CORE, est. ~$250M), neither with terms. Last week Anthropic (ANT) priced 980M shares at $83, above the $70–$78 range, raising $81.34B (plus a $26B private placement), opened +34%, closed day one +17% and sat at $88.91 (+7.1%) after Friday. The Nov 9–13 debuts: Windward Bio (WWB) +42.9% since IPO (first day +67.6%), vVardis (VVVV) -19.2% (first day -8.3%) and Modern Mining (MDRN) -32.9% (first day -3.5%). New filings: Core Specialty (CORE) and SPAC Compute AI (AICPU, $75M). Pulled: Football Manager SPAC postponed; Rezera's earlier postponement stands. Since-IPO returns are from Stock Analysis through the Nov 20 close.",
  "highlights": [
    {
      "text": "Anthropic (ANT) priced at $83, above the $70–$78 range, raising $81.34B in the largest IPO ever; +17% on day one, +7.1% since IPO at the Nov 20 close",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "No US IPOs are scheduled for Thanksgiving week (Nov 23–27)",
      "unconfirmed": false,
      "note": "Renaissance, Nasdaq/NYSE calendars"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tracx Logis (TRCX, $18–$22, ~$20M) and Primagrove (YNTE, $4–$6) are listed for the week of Nov 30",
      "unconfirmed": true,
      "note": "Dates from IPOScoop only"
    },
    {
      "text": "American Barrick Gold (ABGC, est. ~$6B) and Core Specialty (CORE, est. ~$250M) are eligible to launch after Thanksgiving",
      "unconfirmed": true,
      "note": "No terms filed; sizes are Renaissance estimates"
    },
    {
      "text": "Football Manager SPAC (FBLLU, $100M) postponed its Nov 20 IPO; it did not price",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "vVardis (VVVV) is -19.2% and Modern Mining (MDRN) -32.9% since IPO; Windward Bio (WWB) is +42.9%",
      "unconfirmed": false,
